######################################
# product-service — CRUD (direct port 8082)
######################################

### Get all products
GET http://localhost:8082/api/products

###

### Get product by id
GET http://localhost:8082/api/products/1

###

### Create a new product
POST http://localhost:8082/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productCode": "SPORT-003",
  "name": "Tennis Racket",
  "description": "Professional tennis racket",
  "price": 89.99
}

###

### Update product by id
PUT http://localhost:8082/api/products/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productCode": "SPORT-001",
  "name": "Football Pro",
  "description": "Updated professional football",
  "price": 34.99
}

###

### Delete product by id
DELETE http://localhost:8082/api/products/3

######################################
# product-service — with quantity (direct port 8082)
######################################

###

### Get product with quantity (original — calls inventory via WebClient)
GET http://localhost:8082/api/productquantity/1

###

### Get product with quantity — NO resilience (throws raw exception when inventory is down)
GET http://localhost:8082/api/products/quantity/1

######################################
# Resilience4j — Circuit Breaker
# - inventory-service UP   → returns real quantity
# - inventory-service DOWN → returns fallback object immediately (after circuit trips)
# Check CB state: GET http://localhost:8082/actuator/health
# CLOSED=normal  OPEN=tripped  HALF_OPEN=recovering
# Trips OPEN after >= 50% failures in a 5-call window
# Returns to HALF_OPEN after 5 s, then CLOSED after 3 successful calls
######################################

###

### Get product with quantity — Circuit Breaker (port 8082)
GET http://localhost:8082/api/products/quantityCB/1

### Get product with quantity — Circuit Breaker via API Gateway (port 8080)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/products/quantityCB/1

### Check Circuit Breaker health
GET http://localhost:8082/actuator/health

######################################
# Resilience4j — Time Limiter
# inventory-service sleeps 8 s; TimeLimiter fires after 3 s → fallback
# Both inventory UP and DOWN will trigger the fallback (due to the 8s sleep)
######################################

###

### Get product with quantity — Time Limiter
GET http://localhost:8082/api/products/quantityTL/1

######################################
# Resilience4j — Retry
# Retries up to 3 times with 5 s between attempts when inventory is down
# Watch product-service terminal to see each "Retry attempt" log line
######################################

###

### Get product with quantity — Retry
GET http://localhost:8082/api/products/quantityRetry/1

######################################
# Resilience4j — Rate Limiter
# Max 2 requests per 5-second window
# Send 3+ times quickly → 3rd request gets fallback ("rate limit exceeded")
######################################

###

### Get product with quantity — Rate Limiter (send this 3+ times quickly)
GET http://localhost:8082/api/products/quantityRL/1

######################################
# inventory-service — direct (port 8083)
######################################

###

### Get inventory by product code
GET http://localhost:8083/api/inventory/SPORT-001

